{#---------------------------------------------------------------------
   gemma4_fixed_template.jinja
   =====================================
   Fixed chat template for Google's Gemma 4, tuned for open-source
   agentic coding harnesses like:
     - anomalyco/opencode      (https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode)
     - earendil-works/pi       (https://github.com/earendil-works/pi)
     - openclaw, OpenHarness,  similar Claude-Code-style harnesses

   TARGET MODELS
   -------------
   Gemma 4 family (e.g. gemma-4-12B-it, gemma-4-26B-A4B-it, gemma-4-31B-it)
   All sizes/variants that ship the Gemma 4 chat protocol (<|turn>,
   <|think|>, <|channel>thought, <|tool_call>call:name{...} DSL).
   Not intended for Gemma 2 / Gemma 3 (different chat protocols).

   DESIGN PRINCIPLES
   -----------------
   1. Accuracy first — output must match Gemma 4 native turn/channel/tool
      DSL as documented by Google (ai.google.dev/gemma).
   2. Fault tolerance second — accept messy harness inputs (string
      arguments, OpenAI tool envelope, multimodal content parts) and
      render valid prompts; avoid silent corruption over blind fail-fast.
   3. Agent smoothness — defaults tuned for multi-turn tool loops:
      preserve historical <|channel>thought, inject tool-error guidance,
      P5 continuation turns; kwargs can restore upstream parity.
   4. Layered errors — crash only when prompt cannot be made valid;
      warn/guide when tool calls fail; lenient fallback for wire-format
      differences (OpenAI JSON-string arguments).

   BASE
   ----
   Forked from gemma4_improved_template.jinja. All five improved-template
   patches (P1–P5) are preserved unchanged in behaviour. P6 is an additive
   prompt-level thinking-control layer, modelled after:
     froggeric/Qwen-Fixed-Chat-Templates
     https://huggingface.co/froggeric/Qwen-Fixed-Chat-Templates

   COMPATIBILITY WITH gemma4_improved_template.jinja
   -------------------------------------------------
   When you do NOT insert <|think_on|> or <|think_off|> in any message,
   and you do not hit the P6b consecutive-tool-error gen-prompt guard,
   rendered output is byte-for-byte identical to gemma4_improved_template
   on the same inputs (plain chat, system+tools, tool calls, P5
   continuation turns, and enable_thinking=false + preserve_thinking=false
   upstream-compat mode were verified).

   chat_template_kwargs (enable_thinking, preserve_thinking) continue to
   work exactly as in the improved template. P6 tokens are an optional
   override layer on top — they never replace or break the kwargs path.

   PATCH INVENTORY (inherited from gemma4_improved_template.jinja)
   ---------------------------------------------------------------
   P1  format_argument: emit JSON null instead of bare "None"
       Fixes optional tool args (e.g. language=null) rendering as the
       invalid literal "None" in Gemma 4 DSL.

   P2  enable_thinking defaults to TRUE
       Agentic harnesses often cannot pass chat_template_kwargs through
       OpenAI-compatible SDKs; server-side default-on restores tool-call
       accuracy without harness changes.

   P3  tool_call.arguments: lenient string fallback (official parity) with
       opt-in strict_tool_arguments raise and parse_string_arguments expand.

   P4  preserve_thinking kwarg (default TRUE) keeps prior <|channel>thought
       blocks in multi-turn tool loops. Upstream drops reasoning after the
       last user turn, causing arguments:{} collapse on turn 3+.

   P5  fix HF discussion #62 turn-tag close asymmetry
       Suppresses spurious <turn|> closes when consecutive text-only
       assistant messages continue the same model turn frame.

   NEW IN THIS FILE (gemma4_fixed_template.jinja)
   ----------------------------------------------
   P6  Prompt-level thinking control via <|think_on|> and <|think_off|>
       Insert either token anywhere in the first system/developer message
       or in any user message. Tokens are harness directives only — they
       are stripped before rendering and never reach the model tokenizer.

       Priority chain (last wins across the conversation):
         chat_template_kwargs.enable_thinking  (default true, from P2)
           → first system/developer message tokens
           → each subsequent user message token

       Same-message precedence (matches Qwen-Fixed-Chat-Templates):
         system/developer: <|think_on|> wins if both tokens appear
         user messages:    <|think_off|> wins if both tokens appear

       Effect on native Gemma tags (two separate layers, no collision):
         - System turn: <|think|> injected only when thinking is ON at
           system-render time (parsed from first system message before
           injection).
         - Generation prompt: when thinking is OFF, pre-fills an empty
           <|channel>thought\n<channel|> block so the model skips reasoning;
           when ON, opens <|turn>model\n without that pre-fill.

       Gen-prompt state is read from ns_think.enable_thinking (not a
       block-scoped copy) so think_off in the last user turn reliably
       reaches the generation prompt under LM Studio / HF Jinja.

   P6b Side-effect guards (modelled on Qwen-Fixed-Chat-Templates)
       - Parse control tokens ONLY in system/developer + user text.
         Tool payloads are never parsed (source code may contain the
         strings literally).
       - Strip control tokens from all rendered text; never re-parse them
         from assistant reasoning/content round-trips (prevents feedback
         loops when model output is fed back as history).
       - Gate historical <|channel>thought re-emission on
         ns_think.enable_thinking at the assistant turn being rendered.
         Avoids channel/tag clash when a prior user turn disabled thinking.
       - Enhanced strip_thinking: remove malformed/unclosed channel blocks,
         leaked <|think|>, and any control tokens from assistant content.
       - Consecutive tool errors (≥2): force empty <|channel>thought at
         gen prompt to break bad reasoning loops (Qwen-Fixed guard).
         Tool-error warnings are injected into <|tool_response> payloads
         on the first failure; gen-prompt guard fires on ≥2 consecutive.
         Does not affect improved-template output unless this guard fires.

   P7  kwargs (agent-friendly defaults; opt out for upstream parity)
       agent_defaults=true (default): P2 enable_thinking defaults ON.
       strict_tool_arguments=false (default): string args raw-inserted
         inside call:name{...} like official Gemma 4 upstream.
       parse_string_arguments=false (default): when true + from_json
         runtime, JSON strings expand to mapping key:value pairs.
       inject_tool_error_warnings=true (default): P6b warning injection.
       unwrap_tool_envelope=true (default): bare function specs accepted.

   P8  Sync protocol fixes from official gemma4_26b_2607.jinja (2026-07-09)
       Google canonical template: tool-calling loops, turn closures, and
       thinking content-ordering. Agent defaults (P2/P4/P6/P7) unchanged.
       - Gen-prompt after tool_response + thinking ON: open
         <|channel>thought\n (no new <|turn>model), matching official
         multi-turn tool loops. P6b consecutive-error guard still forces
         an empty closed thought channel instead.
       - continues_into_next: allow same model turn when tool_calls were
         already paired with tool_responses (not tool_calls or ns_tr_out).
       - Turn close: suppress <turn|> only when tool_response + empty
         content + no following non-tool message (next_nt.found).
       - Continuation detection: O(1) prev_non_tool_role (no backward scan).
       - Multimodal parts: accept OpenAI image_url / input_audio aliases.
       - Safer .get() for tool_calls / content. Intentionally NOT adopted:
         official enable_thinking/preserve_thinking defaults (false),
         narrow preserve_thinking∧tool_calls gate, or string-args raise.

   UPSTREAM PARITY (chat_template_kwargs)
   --------------------------------------
     {"agent_defaults": false, "enable_thinking": false,
      "preserve_thinking": false, "strict_tool_arguments": true,
      "inject_tool_error_warnings": false}

   preserve_thinking vs official Gemma 4 template
   ----------------------------------------------
     preserve_thinking=true (default)  →  keep all <|channel>thought blocks
     preserve_thinking=false           →  only after last user turn
                                          (plus tool_calls gate for upstream)

   USAGE
   -----
   LM Studio:  My Models → model settings → Prompt Template → paste path
   vLLM/SGLang: --chat-template /path/to/gemma4_fixed_template.jinja
               --tool-call-parser gemma4 --reasoning-parser gemma4

   Tests: python tests/test_gemma4_fixed_chat_template.py

   LM STUDIO / HUGGINGFACE JINJA NOTES
   -----------------------------------
   Think-control logic is inlined in the template body (not passed into
   macros via namespace arguments). Restricted Jinja runtimes used by LM
   Studio and HF reject namespace-as-macro-arg and nested macro calls;
   the inline form matches qwen_fixed_template.jinja and avoids
   "Missing positional argument" render errors.

   THINKING CONTROL — QUICK EXAMPLES
   ---------------------------------
   Disable reasoning for one turn (no SDK changes):
     {"role":"user","content":"<|think_off|>\nAnswer briefly."}

   Re-enable after a prior think_off:
     {"role":"user","content":"<|think_on|>\nNow explain step by step."}

   Force off via kwargs (improved-template path, still works):
     {"extra_body":{"chat_template_kwargs":{"enable_thinking":false}}}

   PINS
   ----
   Upstream:  google/gemma-4-31B-it @ fcf2302760ae9c6e528a8dbba9dd636e56848237
   Protocol:  gemma4_26b_2607.jinja (Google canonical, 2026-07-09)
   Base fork: gemma4_improved_template.jinja
   License:   Apache 2.0 (same as upstream)

---------------------------------------------------------------------#}

{%- macro format_parameters(properties, required, filter_keys=false) -%}
    {%- set standard_keys = ['description', 'type', 'properties', 'required', 'nullable'] -%}
    {%- set ns = namespace(found_first=false) -%}
    {%- for key, value in properties | dictsort -%}
        {%- set add_comma = false -%}
        {%- if not filter_keys or key not in standard_keys -%}
            {%- if ns.found_first %},{% endif -%}
            {%- set ns.found_first = true -%}
            {{ key }}:{
            {%- if value['description'] -%}
                description:<|"|>{{ value['description'] }}<|"|>
                {%- set add_comma = true -%}
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if (value['type'] | default('')) | upper == 'STRING' -%}
                {%- if value['enum'] -%}
                    {%- if add_comma %},{%- else -%} {%- set add_comma = true -%} {% endif -%}
                    enum:{{ format_argument(value['enum']) }}
                {%- endif -%}
            {%- elif (value['type'] | default('')) | upper == 'ARRAY' -%}
                {%- if value['items'] is mapping and value['items'] -%}
                    {%- if add_comma %},{%- else -%} {%- set add_comma = true -%} {% endif -%}
                    items:{
                    {%- set ns_items = namespace(found_first=false) -%}
                    {%- for item_key, item_value in value['items'] | dictsort -%}
                        {%- if item_value is not none -%}
                            {%- if ns_items.found_first %},{% endif -%}
                            {%- set ns_items.found_first = true -%}
                            {%- if item_key == 'properties' -%}
                                properties:{
                                {%- if item_value is mapping -%}
                                    {{- format_parameters(item_value, value['items']['required'] | default([])) -}}
                                {%- endif -%}
                                }
                            {%- elif item_key == 'required' -%}
                                required:[
                                {%- for req_item in item_value -%}
                                    <|"|>{{- req_item -}}<|"|>
                                    {%- if not loop.last %},{% endif -%}
                                {%- endfor -%}
                                ]
                            {%- elif item_key == 'type' -%}
                                {%- if item_value is string -%}
                                    type:{{ format_argument(item_value | upper) }}
                                {%- else -%}
                                    type:{{ format_argument(item_value | map('upper') | list) }}
                                {%- endif -%}
                            {%- else -%}
                                {{ item_key }}:{{ format_argument(item_value) }}
                            {%- endif -%}
                        {%- endif -%}
                    {%- endfor -%}
                    }
                {%- endif -%}
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if value['nullable'] %}
                {%- if add_comma %},{%- else -%} {%- set add_comma = true -%} {% endif -%}
                nullable:true
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if (value['type'] | default('')) | upper == 'OBJECT' -%}
                {%- if value['properties'] is defined and value['properties'] is mapping -%}
                    {%- if add_comma %},{%- else -%} {%- set add_comma = true -%} {% endif -%}
                    properties:{
                    {{- format_parameters(value['properties'], value['required'] | default([])) -}}
                    }
                {%- elif value is mapping -%}
                    {%- if add_comma %},{%- else -%} {%- set add_comma = true -%} {% endif -%}
                    properties:{
                    {{- format_parameters(value, value['required'] | default([]), filter_keys=true) -}}
                    }
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- if value['required'] -%}
                    {%- if add_comma %},{%- else -%} {%- set add_comma = true -%} {% endif -%}
                    required:[
                    {%- for item in value['required'] | default([]) -%}
                        <|"|>{{- item -}}<|"|>
                        {%- if not loop.last %},{% endif -%}
                    {%- endfor -%}
                    ]
                {%- endif -%}
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- if value['type'] is defined and value['type'] is not none -%}
                {%- if add_comma %},{%- else -%} {%- set add_comma = true -%} {% endif -%}
                type:<|"|>{{ value['type'] | upper }}<|"|>
            {%- endif -%}
            }
        {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro format_function_declaration(tool_data) -%}
    declaration:{{- tool_data['function']['name'] -}}{description:<|"|>{{- tool_data['function']['description'] -}}<|"|>
    {%- set params = tool_data['function']['parameters'] -%}
    {%- if params -%}
        ,parameters:{
        {%- if params['properties'] -%}
            properties:{ {{- format_parameters(params['properties'], params['required']) -}} },
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if params['required'] -%}
            required:[
            {%- for item in params['required'] -%}
                <|"|>{{- item -}}<|"|>
                {{- ',' if not loop.last -}}
            {%- endfor -%}
            ],
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if params['type'] is defined and params['type'] is not none -%}
            type:<|"|>{{- params['type'] | upper -}}<|"|>
        {%- endif -%}
        }
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if 'response' in tool_data['function'] -%}
        {%- set response_declaration = tool_data['function']['response'] -%}
        ,response:{
        {%- if response_declaration['description'] -%}
            description:<|"|>{{- response_declaration['description'] -}}<|"|>,
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if (response_declaration['type'] | default('')) | upper == 'OBJECT' -%}
            type:<|"|>{{- response_declaration['type'] | upper -}}<|"|>
        {%- endif -%}
        }
    {%- endif -%}
    }
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro format_argument(argument, escape_keys=True) -%}
    {%- if argument is none -%}
        {{- 'null' -}}
    {%- elif argument is string -%}
        {{- '<|"|>' + argument + '<|"|>' -}}
    {%- elif argument is boolean -%}
        {{- 'true' if argument else 'false' -}}
    {%- elif argument is mapping -%}
        {{- '{' -}}
        {%- set ns = namespace(found_first=false) -%}
        {%- for key, value in argument | dictsort -%}
            {%- if ns.found_first %},{% endif -%}
            {%- set ns.found_first = true -%}
            {%- if escape_keys -%}
                {{- '<|"|>' + key + '<|"|>' -}}
            {%- else -%}
                {{- key -}}
            {%- endif -%}
            :{{- format_argument(value, escape_keys=escape_keys) -}}
        {%- endfor -%}
        {{- '}' -}}
    {%- elif argument is iterable -%}
        {{- '[' -}}
        {%- for item in argument -%}
            {{- format_argument(item, escape_keys=escape_keys) -}}
            {%- if not loop.last %},{% endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
        {{- ']' -}}
    {%- else -%}
        {{- argument -}}
    {%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro strip_think_control_tokens(text) -%}
    {#- P6b: strip harness directives only — never interpret them here.
        Single-arg output macro; safe to call from template body. Do NOT
        call from inside other macros (LM Studio / HF jinja limitation). -#}
    {{- text | replace('<|think_off|>', '') | replace('<|think_on|>', '') | trim -}}
{%- endmacro -%}
{%- macro strip_thinking(text) -%}
    {#- P6b: remove Gemma 4 <|channel>thought blocks from assistant
        content round-trips. Inlined token strip (no nested macro calls). -#}
    {%- set text = text | replace('<|think_off|>', '') | replace('<|think_on|>', '') | trim -%}
    {%- set ns = namespace(result='') -%}
    {%- for part in text.split('<channel|>') -%}
        {%- if '<|channel>' in part -%}
            {%- set ns.result = ns.result + part.split('<|channel>')[0] -%}
        {%- else -%}
            {%- set ns.result = ns.result + part -%}
        {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
    {%- set text = ns.result -%}
    {%- if '<|channel>thought' in text -%}
        {%- set text = text.split('<|channel>thought')[0] -%}
    {%- elif '<|channel> thought' in text -%}
        {%- set text = text.split('<|channel> thought')[0] -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- set text = text | replace('<|think|>', '') | replace('<|think|>\n', '') -%}
    {{- text | trim -}}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- macro format_tool_response_block(tool_name, response) -%}
    {{- '<|tool_response>' -}}
    {%- if response is mapping -%}
        {{- 'response:' + tool_name + '{' -}}
        {%- for key, value in response | dictsort -%}
            {{- key -}}:{{- format_argument(value, escape_keys=False) -}}
            {%- if not loop.last %},{% endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
        {{- '}' -}}
    {%- else -%}
        {{- 'response:' + tool_name + '{value:' + format_argument(response, escape_keys=False) + '}' -}}
    {%- endif -%}
    {{- '<tool_response|>' -}}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- P6b: probe tool payload, update consecutive-failure counters, optionally
    append SYSTEM WARNING into the value rendered inside <|tool_response>. -#}
{%- macro render_tool_response_with_error_guard(tool_name, tool_body) -%}
    {%- set probe = tool_body | string -%}
    {%- set probe_lower = probe | lower -%}
    {%- set is_tool_error = false -%}
    {%- if probe | length < 500
        and '$ ' not in probe
        and 'took ' not in probe_lower
        and ('"error": true' in probe_lower or '"error":true' in probe_lower
             or '"error": "' in probe_lower or '"error":"' in probe_lower
             or '"status": "error"' in probe_lower or '"status":"error"' in probe_lower
             or 'exception:' in probe_lower or 'traceback' in probe_lower
             or 'command not found' in probe_lower or 'invalid syntax' in probe_lower
             or 'failed to' in probe_lower) -%}
        {%- set is_tool_error = true -%}
        {%- set ns_toolfail.last_tool_failed = true -%}
        {%- set ns_toolfail.consecutive_failures = ns_toolfail.consecutive_failures + 1 -%}
    {%- else -%}
        {%- set ns_toolfail.last_tool_failed = false -%}
        {%- set ns_toolfail.consecutive_failures = 0 -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if is_tool_error and (inject_tool_error_warnings is not defined or inject_tool_error_warnings is not false) -%}
        {%- if ns_toolfail.consecutive_failures >= 2 -%}
            {%- set probe = probe ~ '\n\n⚠️ SYSTEM WARNING: ' ~ ns_toolfail.consecutive_failures ~ ' consecutive tool errors detected. Your previous approach is incorrect. You MUST use a fundamentally different approach or corrected arguments.' -%}
        {%- else -%}
            {%- set probe = probe ~ '\n\n⚠️ SYSTEM WARNING: The previous tool call returned an error. Diagnose the failure and retry with completely corrected arguments.' -%}
        {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {{- format_tool_response_block(tool_name, probe) -}}
{%- endmacro -%}

{%- set ns = namespace(prev_message_type=None, prev_non_tool_role=None) -%}
{%- set loop_messages = messages -%}
{%- set ns_toolfail = namespace(last_tool_failed=false, consecutive_failures=0) -%}

{%- if not messages -%}
    {{- raise_exception('No messages provided.') -}}
{%- endif -%}

{#- P7: agent_defaults=true keeps P2 server-side enable_thinking default-on.
    Set agent_defaults=false to recover upstream "undefined = off" semantics. -#}
{%- if agent_defaults is defined and agent_defaults is false -%}
    {%- if enable_thinking is defined -%}
        {%- set enable_thinking = enable_thinking -%}
    {%- else -%}
        {%- set enable_thinking = false -%}
    {%- endif -%}
{%- else -%}
    {%- set enable_thinking = enable_thinking | default(true) -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- set ns_think = namespace(enable_thinking=enable_thinking) -%}

{#- P6: parse think control tokens from the first system/developer
    message BEFORE deciding whether to inject <|think|> in the system
    turn. Uses system precedence (think_on wins). -#}
{%- set ns_sys_probe = namespace(text='') -%}
{%- if messages[0]['role'] in ['system', 'developer'] -%}
    {%- if messages[0]['content'] is string -%}
        {%- set ns_sys_probe.text = messages[0]['content'] -%}
    {%- elif messages[0]['content'] is iterable -%}
        {%- for item in messages[0]['content'] -%}
            {%- if item['type'] == 'text' -%}
                {%- set ns_sys_probe.text = ns_sys_probe.text + item['text'] -%}
            {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {#- P6 inline (system path): think_on wins when both present. -#}
    {%- if '<|think_off|>' in ns_sys_probe.text -%}
        {%- set ns_think.enable_thinking = false -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if '<|think_on|>' in ns_sys_probe.text -%}
        {%- set ns_think.enable_thinking = true -%}
    {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- set enable_thinking = ns_think.enable_thinking -%}

{{- bos_token -}}
{#- Handle System/Tool Definitions Block -#}
{%- if enable_thinking or tools or messages[0]['role'] in ['system', 'developer'] -%}
    {{- '<|turn>system\n' -}}
    {%- if enable_thinking -%}
        {{- '<|think|>\n' -}}
        {%- set ns.prev_message_type = 'think' -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if messages[0]['role'] in ['system', 'developer'] -%}
        {%- if messages[0]['content'] is string -%}
            {{- strip_think_control_tokens(messages[0]['content']) -}}
        {%- elif messages[0]['content'] is iterable -%}
            {%- for item in messages[0]['content'] -%}
                {%- if item['type'] == 'text' -%}
                    {{- strip_think_control_tokens(item['text']) + ' ' -}}
                {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- set loop_messages = messages[1:] -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if tools -%}
        {%- for tool in tools %}
            {%- if tool.function is defined -%}
                {%- set tool_decl = tool -%}
            {%- elif unwrap_tool_envelope is defined and unwrap_tool_envelope is false -%}
                {%- set tool_decl = tool -%}
            {%- else -%}
                {%- set tool_decl = {'function': tool} -%}
            {%- endif -%}
            {{- '<|tool>' -}}
            {{- format_function_declaration(tool_decl) | trim -}}
            {{- '<tool|>' -}}
        {%- endfor %}
        {%- set ns.prev_message_type = 'tool' -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {{- '<turn|>\n' -}}
{%- endif %}

{%- set preserve_thinking = preserve_thinking | default(true) -%}

{#- Pre-scan: find last user message index for reasoning guard -#}
{%- set ns_turn = namespace(last_user_idx=-1) -%}
{%- for i in range(loop_messages | length) -%}
    {%- if loop_messages[i]['role'] == 'user' -%}
        {%- set ns_turn.last_user_idx = i -%}
    {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{#- Loop through messages -#}
{%- for message in loop_messages -%}
    {%- if message['role'] != 'tool' -%}
    {%- set ns.prev_message_type = None -%}
    {%- set role = 'model' if message['role'] == 'assistant' else message['role'] -%}
    {#- P8: O(1) continuation via prev_non_tool_role (official 2607) -#}
    {%- set continue_same_model_turn = (role == 'model' and ns.prev_non_tool_role == 'assistant') -%}
    {%- if not continue_same_model_turn -%}
        {{- '<|turn>' + role + '\n' }}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- set thinking_text = message.get('reasoning') or message.get('reasoning_content') -%}
    {%- if thinking_text is string -%}
        {%- set thinking_text = thinking_text | replace('<|think_off|>', '') | replace('<|think_on|>', '') | trim -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- set thinking_gate = (loop.index0 > ns_turn.last_user_idx) or preserve_thinking -%}
    {#- P4 fix: preserve_thinking keeps <|channel>thought even without tool_calls.
        Upstream only emits thinking when tool_calls exist; agent harnesses need
        reasoning_content preserved on plain assistant turns too. -#}
    {%- set emit_thinking = false -%}
    {%- if thinking_text and thinking_gate and ns_think.enable_thinking -%}
        {%- if message.get('tool_calls') or preserve_thinking -%}
            {%- set emit_thinking = true -%}
        {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {#- P6b: when enable_thinking is false at this point in history, omit
        the <|channel>thought block entirely (Qwen-Fixed show_think gate).
        Prevents native channel tags from colliding with think_off turns. -#}
    {%- if emit_thinking -%}
        {{- '<|channel>thought\n' + thinking_text + '\n<channel|>' -}}
    {%- endif -%}

            {%- if message.get('tool_calls') -%}
                {%- for tool_call in message.get('tool_calls') -%}
                    {%- set function = tool_call['function'] -%}
                    {{- '<|tool_call>call:' + function['name'] + '{' -}}
                    {%- if function['arguments'] is mapping -%}
                        {%- set ns_args = namespace(found_first=false) -%}
                        {%- for key, value in function['arguments'] | dictsort -%}
                            {%- if ns_args.found_first %},{% endif -%}
                            {%- set ns_args.found_first = true -%}
                            {{- key -}}:{{- format_argument(value, escape_keys=False) -}}
                        {%- endfor -%}
                    {%- elif function['arguments'] is none -%}
                    {%- elif function['arguments'] is string -%}
                        {%- set arg_string = function['arguments'] | trim -%}
                        {%- if strict_tool_arguments is defined and strict_tool_arguments -%}
                            {{- raise_exception(
                                "gemma4_fixed_template: "
                                "tool_calls[].function.arguments must be a JSON "
                                "object (mapping). Got a string. Deserialize once "
                                "on ingest, set parse_string_arguments=true on "
                                "runtimes with from_json, or omit strict_tool_arguments."
                            ) -}}
                        {%- elif parse_string_arguments is defined and parse_string_arguments and arg_string | length > 0 -%}
                            {%- set parsed_args = arg_string | from_json -%}
                            {%- if parsed_args is mapping -%}
                                {%- set ns_args = namespace(found_first=false) -%}
                                {%- for key, value in parsed_args | dictsort -%}
                                    {%- if ns_args.found_first %},{% endif -%}
                                    {%- set ns_args.found_first = true -%}
                                    {{- key -}}:{{- format_argument(value, escape_keys=False) -}}
                                {%- endfor -%}
                            {%- else -%}
                                {{- arg_string -}}
                            {%- endif -%}
                        {%- elif arg_string | length > 0 -%}
                            {{- arg_string -}}
                        {%- endif -%}
                    {%- else -%}
                        {{- raise_exception(
                            "gemma4_fixed_template: "
                            "tool_calls[].function.arguments must be a JSON "
                            "object (mapping). Got a non-mapping value. "
                            "This is almost always the harness handing back "
                            "a JSON-encoded STRING rather than the deserialized "
                            "object. Deserialize once on ingest and store the "
                            "object. See: github.com/earendil-works/pi/issues/3325"
                        ) -}}
                    {%- endif -%}
                    {{- '}<tool_call|>' -}}
                {%- endfor -%}
                {%- set ns.prev_message_type = 'tool_call' -%}
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- set ns_tr_out = namespace(flag=false) -%}
            {%- if message.get('tool_responses') -%}
                {%- for tool_response in message.get('tool_responses') -%}
                    {%- set tr_body = tool_response['response'] -%}
                    {%- if tr_body is mapping -%}
                        {{- format_tool_response_block(tool_response['name'] | default('unknown', true), tr_body) -}}
                    {%- else -%}
                        {{- render_tool_response_with_error_guard(tool_response['name'] | default('unknown', true), tr_body) -}}
                    {%- endif -%}
                    {%- set ns_tr_out.flag = true -%}
                    {%- set ns.prev_message_type = 'tool_response' -%}
                {%- endfor -%}
            {%- elif message.get('tool_calls') -%}
                {%- set ns_tool_scan = namespace(stopped=false) -%}
                {%- for k in range(loop.index0 + 1, loop_messages | length) -%}
                    {%- if ns_tool_scan.stopped -%}
                    {%- elif loop_messages[k]['role'] != 'tool' -%}
                        {%- set ns_tool_scan.stopped = true -%}
                    {%- else -%}
                        {%- set follow = loop_messages[k] -%}
                        {%- set ns_tname = namespace(name=follow.get('name') or 'unknown') -%}
                        {%- for tc in message.get('tool_calls') -%}
                            {%- if tc.get('id') == follow.get('tool_call_id') -%}
                                {%- set ns_tname.name = tc['function']['name'] -%}
                            {%- endif -%}
                        {%- endfor -%}
                        {%- set tool_body = follow.get('content') -%}
                        {%- if tool_body is string -%}
                            {{- render_tool_response_with_error_guard(ns_tname.name, tool_body) -}}
                        {%- elif tool_body is iterable and tool_body is not string -%}
                            {%- set ns_txt = namespace(s='') -%}
                            {%- for part in tool_body -%}
                                {%- if part.get('type') == 'text' -%}
                                    {%- set ns_txt.s = ns_txt.s + (part.get('text') | default('')) -%}
                                {%- endif -%}
                            {%- endfor -%}
                            {{- render_tool_response_with_error_guard(ns_tname.name, ns_txt.s) -}}
                            {%- for part in tool_body -%}
                                {%- if part.get('type') in ['image', 'image_url'] -%}
                                    {{- '<|image|>' -}}
                                {%- elif part.get('type') in ['audio', 'input_audio'] -%}
                                    {{- '<|audio|>' -}}
                                {%- elif part.get('type') == 'video' -%}
                                    {{- '<|video|>' -}}
                                {%- endif -%}
                            {%- endfor -%}
                        {%- else -%}
                            {{- render_tool_response_with_error_guard(ns_tname.name, tool_body) -}}
                        {%- endif -%}
                        {%- set ns_tr_out.flag = true -%}
                        {%- set ns.prev_message_type = 'tool_response' -%}
                    {%- endif -%}
                {%- endfor -%}
            {%- endif -%}

            {%- set captured_content -%}
            {%- if message.get('content') is string -%}
                {%- if role == 'model' -%}
                    {{- strip_thinking(message['content']) -}}
                {%- elif role == 'user' -%}
                    {%- set user_text = message['content'] -%}
                    {%- if '<|think_off|>' in user_text -%}
                        {%- set ns_think.enable_thinking = false -%}
                        {%- set user_text = user_text | replace('<|think_off|>', '') | trim -%}
                    {%- elif '<|think_on|>' in user_text -%}
                        {%- set ns_think.enable_thinking = true -%}
                        {%- set user_text = user_text | replace('<|think_on|>', '') | trim -%}
                    {%- else -%}
                        {%- set user_text = user_text | trim -%}
                    {%- endif -%}
                    {%- set enable_thinking = ns_think.enable_thinking -%}
                    {{- user_text -}}
                {%- else -%}
                    {{- message['content'] | trim -}}
                {%- endif -%}
            {%- elif message.get('content') is iterable -%}
                {%- for item in message['content'] -%}
                    {%- if item.get('type') == 'text' -%}
                        {%- if role == 'model' -%}
                            {{- strip_thinking(item['text']) -}}
                        {%- elif role == 'user' -%}
                            {%- set user_text = item['text'] -%}
                            {%- if '<|think_off|>' in user_text -%}
                                {%- set ns_think.enable_thinking = false -%}
                                {%- set user_text = user_text | replace('<|think_off|>', '') | trim -%}
                            {%- elif '<|think_on|>' in user_text -%}
                                {%- set ns_think.enable_thinking = true -%}
                                {%- set user_text = user_text | replace('<|think_on|>', '') | trim -%}
                            {%- else -%}
                                {%- set user_text = user_text | trim -%}
                            {%- endif -%}
                            {%- set enable_thinking = ns_think.enable_thinking -%}
                            {{- user_text -}}
                        {%- else -%}
                            {{- item['text'] | trim -}}
                        {%- endif -%}
                    {%- elif item.get('type') in ['image', 'image_url'] -%}
                        {{- '<|image|>' -}}
                        {%- set ns.prev_message_type = 'image' -%}
                    {%- elif item.get('type') in ['audio', 'input_audio'] -%}
                        {{- '<|audio|>' -}}
                        {%- set ns.prev_message_type = 'audio' -%}
                    {%- elif item.get('type') == 'video' -%}
                        {{- '<|video|>' -}}
                        {%- set ns.prev_message_type = 'video' -%}
                    {%- endif -%}
                {%- endfor -%}
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- endset -%}

            {{- captured_content -}}
            {%- if role == 'user' -%}
                {%- set ns_toolfail.last_tool_failed = false -%}
                {%- set ns_toolfail.consecutive_failures = 0 -%}
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- set has_content = captured_content | trim | length > 0 -%}

        {#- P8: forward-scan next non-tool role (official 2607 turn closure) -#}
        {%- set next_nt = namespace(role=None, found=false) -%}
        {%- for j in range(loop.index0 + 1, loop_messages | length) -%}
            {%- if not next_nt.found -%}
                {%- if loop_messages[j]['role'] != 'tool' -%}
                    {%- set next_nt.role = loop_messages[j]['role'] -%}
                    {%- set next_nt.found = true -%}
                {%- endif -%}
            {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
        {%- set continues_into_next = (
            role == 'model'
            and next_nt.role == 'assistant'
            and (not message.get('tool_calls') or ns_tr_out.flag)
        ) -%}

        {%- if ns.prev_message_type == 'tool_call' and not ns_tr_out.flag -%}
            {{- '<|tool_response>' -}}
        {%- elif continues_into_next -%}
        {%- elif not (ns_tr_out.flag and not has_content and not next_nt.found) -%}
            {{- '<turn|>\n' -}}
        {%- endif -%}

    {#- P8: track previous non-tool role for O(1) continuation -#}
    {%- set ns.prev_non_tool_role = message['role'] -%}
    {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- if add_generation_prompt -%}
    {%- if ns.prev_message_type != 'tool_response' and ns.prev_message_type != 'tool_call' -%}
        {{- '<|turn>model\n' -}}
        {#- P6b: pre-fill empty thought channel when thinking is off OR
            when consecutive tool errors suggest the model is stuck in a
            bad reasoning loop (Qwen-Fixed gen-prompt guard). Keeps the
            native Gemma channel frame balanced without free-form thought. -#}
        {%- if not ns_think.enable_thinking -%}
            {{- '<|channel>thought\n<channel|>' -}}
        {%- elif ns_toolfail.last_tool_failed and ns_toolfail.consecutive_failures >= 2 -%}
            {{- '<|channel>thought\n<channel|>' -}}
        {%- endif -%}
    {%- elif ns.prev_message_type == 'tool_response' -%}
        {#- P8 / official 2607: after tool_response, continue the open model
            turn with an open thought channel when thinking is ON. P6b
            consecutive-error guard still forces empty closed thought. -#}
        {%- if ns_think.enable_thinking -%}
            {%- if ns_toolfail.last_tool_failed and ns_toolfail.consecutive_failures >= 2 -%}
                {{- '<|channel>thought\n<channel|>' -}}
            {%- else -%}
                {{- '<|channel>thought\n' -}}
            {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
